# Optimum notices

## Anego Studios

Optimum builds against Vintage Story and uses source repositories published by
Anego Studios as a patch and source baseline. The Anego-derived material is
not covered by `LICENSE-MIT`. It remains subject to
`LICENSE-OPTIMUM-LEGACY-GPL-COMMONS` and the applicable upstream license and
notice files.

The Anego source repositories used by `forks.json` include `vsapi`, `Cairo`,
`vsessentialsmod`, `vssurvivalmod`, and `vscreativemod`. Their upstream license
files identify the software as proprietary. This notice records provenance; it
does not grant permission to redistribute Anego-owned material.

## Third-party material

The optional game-side performance ports in `VulkanStory.Game/Performance`
adapt optimization ideas and patch logic from `_ref/Optimum/patches` and
`_ref/Optimum/sources`, including inventory rendering, weather lookup caching,
block animation LOD, entity retessellation, dynamic-light selection, chunk
visibility and pathfinding node pooling. The historical license and applicable
upstream notices above remain attached to this material. The official game
assemblies are compile-time references and are not redistributed.

Outfit animator layouts, Terrain worker workspaces, physics collection reuse,
chisel LOD routing and world-map page rendering/cache behavior also follow the
Optimum patch/source overlays, with Vulkan-owned rendering and side-table state
in the rewrite. The original material's license scope remains applicable.

Third-party files keep their own notices and license terms. In particular,
`sources/shaders/cloudvolumetric.fsh` contains its own MIT notice for the
Inigo Quilez material it uses.
